* AIF-120 R73 -- the canonical schema in four flavors, and who chooses the index.
*
* WORKSPACE OPEN's usage text says: "Without CNX/INX/CDX, indexes are chosen by
* DBF flavor: true x64/v128 CDX, classic VFP/v32 CNX." Contract 4c lets a UIDEF
* document say Order = inx | cnx, i.e. name the format. This asks the engine
* whether that is the document's choice to make.
*
* One table, STUDENTS, four flavors. Read-only.

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

ECHO
ECHO === og (MS-DOS lineage) ===
SET PATH DBF flav/og
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
AREA

ECHO
ECHO === vfp ===
SET PATH DBF flav/vfp
SELECT 2
USE STUDENTS
AREA

ECHO
ECHO === x32 ===
SET PATH DBF flav/x32
SELECT 3
USE STUDENTS
AREA

ECHO
ECHO === x64 ===
SET PATH DBF dbf/x64
SELECT 4
USE STUDENTS
AREA

WORKSPACE CLOSE
